# Phase 5 T-U1/T-U2 across a width change, with its own turns: the anchor
# turn's command sleeps 20 s, so every snap until `full-pgup-after` is taken
# while it runs and the record is still. At 120 columns: the tail, a page up,
# three rows up and back. Narrowed to 80 with Ctrl-O up (every entry is laid
# out again and the wrapped heading takes more rows): the pinned view, then
# the tail at 80 and a page above it. Widened back to 120: the pinned view,
# the tail and a page above it; then the command settles under that view.
# A width change is a rebuild on fx's screen: the page laid out at the old
# width is the one the position is pinned on (`presentationForRebuiltPage`,
# src/ui/transcript/runtime.zig:11584-11590@481104fd). fx's `shell`/`run` is
# xfx's `terminal`/`exec`; TZ=UTC on both (T-U5).
fx: gateway p5-transcript-resize-turns.json
xfx: gateway p5-transcript-resize-xfx.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
env TZ=UTC
work p5-transcript-ws
wait 4
type read and wait
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-running
key PPage
wait 0.8
snap full-pgup
key Up
wait 0.5
snap full-pgup-up
key Down
wait 0.5
snap full-pgup-back
resize 40x80
wait 1.2
snap full-pgup-80
key NPage NPage NPage
wait 0.8
snap full-tail-80
key PPage
wait 0.8
snap full-tail-80-pgup
resize 40x120
wait 1.2
snap full-pgup-120
key NPage NPage NPage
wait 0.8
snap full-tail-120
key PPage
wait 0.8
snap full-tail-120-pgup
wait 12
snap full-pgup-after
key C-o
wait 1
gwlog
